-- title:
--   Ω_{S/A} is free of rank one on dt
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a commutative domain which is a discrete valuation ring and let $\varpi \in A$ be an element generating its maximal ideal, $\mathfrak{m}_A = (\varpi)$. Let $S$ be a commutative local domain and let $i : A \to S$ be a ring homomorphism which is formally smooth and essentially of finite type, and such that the composite of $i$ with the residue map $S \to S/\mathfrak{m}_S$ is surjective (so the closed point of $S$ is rational over the image of $A$). Let $t \in S$ be such that $\mathfrak{m}_S = (i(\varpi), t)$ and $t \notin (i(\varpi))$. Then, for the $A$-algebra structure on $S$ given by $i$, every element $\omega$ of the module $\Omega_{S/A}$ of Kähler differentials can be written as $\omega = s \cdot \mathrm{d}t$ for a unique $s \in S$; that is, $\mathrm{d}t$ is a basis of $\Omega_{S/A}$ over $S$, so $\Omega_{S/A}$ is free of rank one. The uniqueness half is asserted in the $\exists!$ form rather than as a statement about a chosen basis.
--
--   This is the local computation of the differentials of a smooth relative curve over a discrete valuation ring at a rational closed point of the special fibre: the maximal ideal being generated by the uniformiser together with one further element $t$ forces $\Omega_{S/A}$ to be free on $\mathrm{d}t$. It is used in the proof of [`RingHom.formallySmooth_and_formallyUnramified_eval2RingHom_of_maximalIdeal_eq_span_pair`](thm.html#RingHom.formallySmooth_and_formallyUnramified_eval2RingHom_of_maximalIdeal_eq_span_pair).
